This product includes software developed at the following projects:

- Swarm Bee (https://github.com/ethersphere/bee)
  Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License.
  Used as the base Docker image (ethersphere/bee) for the queen and worker
  services defined in bee/Dockerfile and compose.yml.

- ethersphere/storage-incentives (https://github.com/ethersphere/storage-incentives)
  Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License.
  Solidity sources for the PostageStamp, PriceOracle, StakeRegistry and
  Redistribution contracts. Pulled in via git submodule under
  blockchain/deploy/lib/storage-incentives, compiled by blockchain/deploy
  and deployed at snapshot-bake time by blockchain/bake/deploy-swarm.ts;
  the resulting bytecode + storage live in blockchain/state.gnosis.json.

- OpenZeppelin Contracts (https://github.com/OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts)
  Copyright (c) OpenZeppelin. Licensed under the MIT License.
  Vendored as a git submodule at v4.8.3, used by storage-incentives.
  Imports from this library are embedded into the deployed contract
  bytecode in blockchain/state.gnosis.json.

- Gnosis mainnet state (https://gnosischain.com)
  blockchain/state.gnosis.json also contains storage and bytecode read from
  Gnosis mainnet at bake time for the BZZ token, WXDAI and the SushiSwap V3
  router, quoter and BZZ/WXDAI pool, so the offline chain carries a real BZZ
  market. See blockchain/HYBRID-CHAIN.md.

- fdp-play (https://github.com/fairDataSociety/fdp-play)
  Copyright (c) Fair Data Society. Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License.
  bee/data/{queen,worker-N}/ contains deterministic libp2p / swarm / pss
  keys originally generated by fdp-play. The Ethereum addresses derived
  from those swarm keys are funded with xDAI for gas at snapshot-bake time.

- Foundry / Anvil (https://github.com/foundry-rs/foundry)
  Copyright (c) Foundry contributors. Licensed under the Apache License 2.0
  and MIT License (dual-licensed). Used as the runtime base image for the
  blockchain service (ghcr.io/foundry-rs/foundry) and as the build-time
  toolchain that compiles the contracts and hosts the anvil instances
  blockchain/bake/bake.sh drives to produce blockchain/state.gnosis.json.
